<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for March 8.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for March 8.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas consumption for the period March 6-8.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 6 (actual) 263 mcm, 62 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 7 (forecast) 253 mcm, 59 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 8 (forecast) 234 mcm, 55 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 6 (actual) 7.3 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.6 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 7 (forecast) 8.8 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.7 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 8 (forecast) 7.9 Celsius, seasonal normal 5.8 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Friday, and the probability on Saturday is low.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
